<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ottoman–Safavid War (1532–1555)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1532">1532</a>–<a href="/years/1555">1555</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ottoman–Safavid War of 1532–1555 was fought between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suleiman-the-magnificent">Suleiman the Magnificent</a> and Safavid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tahmasp-i">Tahmasp I</a>. Suleiman led three campaigns into Persia and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> and much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> in 1534; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-amasya">Peace of Amasya</a> (1555), the first formal treaty between the two empires, left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> to the Ottomans and divided the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ottoman-safavid-war-1532-1555.jpg" alt="Ottoman–Safavid War (1532–1555)" width="320" height="439" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nakkaş Osman · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Istanbul,_Topkapi_Palace_Museum_MS_Hazine_1517_fol._592r_Campaign_on_Nachivan_in_the_South_Caucasus.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
